-running/events/316207755/","description":"**Join us for the 10th Anniversary of the Art In Motion 10K/5K/2K!**\nRun or walk with us at Boyd Conservation Area in Vaughan for a community race supporting children and youth living with arthritis.\n\nChoose from the **10K, 5K or 2K** and enjoy a full race-day experience including finisher medals for 10K & 5K participants, professional race photos, post-race refreshments, pancake breakfast, complimentary massages, and more.\n\n**Sunday, October 18, 2026**\n**Boyd Conservation Area • Vaughan, Ontario**\n\n100% of event proceeds support **SickKids Foundation and the Dr. Bonnie Cameron Post-Secondary Scholarship**, helping children and youth living with arthritis receive exceptional care and pursue their educational goals.\n\n**Important:** Joining this Meetup does **not** register you for the race.\n👉 **Race details & official registration:**\n**[https://artinmotion10k.com/](https://artinmotion10k.com/)**","startDate":"2026-10-18T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Boyd Conservation Area","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Vaughan","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"8739 Islington Avenue, Vaughan, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Artinmotion running","url":"https://www.meetup.com/artinmotion-running/"},"performer":"Artinmotion running"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231807/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":" 🌿 FALL WALK -  Walk: Tommy Thompson Park (Come See The Skyline) 🐦 - 12KM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316183191/","description":"# 🍂🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thompson Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife, Lake Views & One of Toronto's Best Fall Walks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you've left the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall walk through **Tommy Thompson Park**, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor spaces.\nThe park is famous for its wildlife and birding, with **more than 300 species recorded**, as well as its beautiful views across Lake Ontario and back toward the Toronto skyline.\nIn the fall, the cooler air and quieter trails make this a particularly nice time to explore the park. We'll follow the trails toward the **lighthouse**, take a break along the way, and then make our way back.\n\nIt's a **long walk**, but the terrain is generally easy. The goal is to enjoy the scenery, get some fresh air, and spend a few hours walking and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near the pavilion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson Park.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look for birds and other wildlife 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* Take in the Toronto skyline 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* Stop for a break and some photos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe walk will take approximately **3 hours, including a break**.\nThis is a longer walk, so you should be comfortable walking at a steady pace for several hours.\n**No dogs are permitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, and Tommy Thompson can be exposed to the wind coming off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and bring comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn't particularly difficult, but **the distance is the challenge**. If you're not comfortable being on your feet and walking steadily for around three hours, this may not be the right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce we've finished, you're welcome to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Hortons** nearby.\nIt's completely optional, but it's a great chance to sit down, refuel, and continue the conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦\n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* People who love waterfront walks\n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\n* People who want to explore somewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who enjoys getting outside and meeting new people\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife.** 🐦\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion -TTC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"9 Leslie Lookout Park, Toronto, ON M4M 3H7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"generative ai art jam","url":"https://www.meetup.com/deployed-ai-downtown-toronto/events/316750063/","description":"Come make art using your favourite ai tool. Easels and paintbrushes not included.","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Dialog Cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"106 Mutual St Unit #8, Toronto, ON M5B 2R7, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Deployed AI Downtown Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/deployed-ai-downtown-toronto/"},"performer":"Deployed AI Downtown Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🌿 FALL WALK -  Walk: Tommy Thompson Park (Come See The Skyline) 🐦 - 12KM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316183196/","description":"# 🍂🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thompson Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife, Lake Views & One of Toronto's Best Fall Walks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you've left the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall walk through **Tommy Thompson Park**, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor spaces.\nThe park is famous for its wildlife and birding, with **more than 300 species recorded**, as well as its beautiful views across Lake Ontario and back toward the Toronto skyline.\nIn the fall, the cooler air and quieter trails make this a particularly nice time to explore the park. We'll follow the trails toward the **lighthouse**, take a break along the way, and then make our way back.\n\nIt's a **long walk**, but the terrain is generally easy. The goal is to enjoy the scenery, get some fresh air, and spend a few hours walking and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near the pavilion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson Park.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look for birds and other wildlife 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* Take in the Toronto skyline 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* Stop for a break and some photos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe walk will take approximately **3 hours, including a break**.\nThis is a longer walk, so you should be comfortable walking at a steady pace for several hours.\n**No dogs are permitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, and Tommy Thompson can be exposed to the wind coming off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and bring comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn't particularly difficult, but **the distance is the challenge**. If you're not comfortable being on your feet and walking steadily for around three hours, this may not be the right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce we've finished, you're welcome to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Hortons** nearby.\nIt's completely optional, but it's a great chance to sit down, refuel, and continue the conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦\n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* People who love waterfront walks\n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\n* People who want to explore somewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who enjoys getting outside and meeting new people\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife.** 🐦\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion -TTC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"9 Leslie Lookout Park, Toronto, ON M4M 3H7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Muskoka cranberry plunge + Hardy Lake","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-wanderers-club-group-trips-for-active-travellers/events/316757128/","description":"This is one for the Gram. We'll be heading Northbound to the Muskoka area for a fun day out in the beautiful Fall color season. We'll start the day by visiting Gravenhurst which is a town in the Muskoka region, here you will have free time to grab some brunch.\n\nAfter that, we'll head over to the Muskoka Lakes Farm and Winery for a popular Fall time activity. You'll be given some chest waders so you can sink into the water surrounded by millions of Cranberries - it's a great way to get those awesome images.\n\nAfter the farm, we'll make a quick stop at a local brewery, followed by Hardy Lake Provincial Park. This small Provincial Park in Muskoka is a must do for those who like hiking. While there are many trails, we'll head on the biggest and best around Hardy Lake which will serve up some good snaps. We'll gage the groups ability and pick the most suitable hike for the day.\n\nPlease email sandra@origin-travels.com for more details and to grab a spot! We will have max 15 people on this day trip.","startDate":"2026-10-18T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Yorkdale TTC Passenger Pick-up","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5234 William R. Allen Rd, North York, ON M6A 3A1, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Wanderer's Club: group trips for active travellers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-wanderers-club-group-trips-for-active-travellers/"},"performer":"The Wanderer's Club: gr