Skyline) 🐦 - 12KM","dateTime":"2026-10-18T11:00:00-04:00","description":"# 🍂🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thompson Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife, Lake Views \u0026 One of Toronto's Best Fall Walks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you've left the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall walk through **Tommy Thompson Park**, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor spaces.\nThe park is famous for its wildlife and birding, with **more than 300 species recorded**, as well as its beautiful views across Lake Ontario and back toward the Toronto skyline.\nIn the fall, the cooler air and quieter trails make this a particularly nice time to explore the park. We'll follow the trails toward the **lighthouse**, take a break along the way, and then make our way back.\n\nIt's a **long walk**, but the terrain is generally easy. The goal is to enjoy the scenery, get some fresh air, and spend a few hours walking and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near the pavilion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson Park.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look for birds and other wildlife 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* Take in the Toronto skyline 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* Stop for a break and some photos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe walk will take approximately **3 hours, including a break**.\nThis is a longer walk, so you should be comfortable walking at a steady pace for several hours.\n**No dogs are permitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather \u0026 Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, and Tommy Thompson can be exposed to the wind coming off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and bring comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn't particularly difficult, but **the distance is the challenge**. If you're not comfortable being on your feet and walking steadily for around three hours, this may not be the right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce we've finished, you're welcome to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Hortons** nearby.\nIt's completely optional, but it's a great chance to sit down, refuel, and continue the conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦\n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* People who love waterfront walks\n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\n* People who want to explore somewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who enjoys getting outside and meeting new people\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife.** 🐦\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316183191/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTic